<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Testour</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Testour is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medjerda">Medjerda River</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>. It was founded in the early 17th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> refugees expelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and its Great Mosque has a minaret in Aragonese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudejar">Mudéjar</a> style with a clock that runs backwards. The town remains a centre of the Andalusian musical tradition known as malouf.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/testour.jpg" alt="Testour" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Noomen9 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grande_Mosqu%C3%A9e_de_Testour_31.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
